{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:27:22Z","thinking":"**Re-evaluating Queue Retry Monitor Status**\n\nAll other actions were synthetic. Need to thoroughly examine all associated records, evidence, and current state. The user requests continued monitoring of the queue retry fix after PR 842 due to a timeout report and a suggestion that monitoring could close.\n\n\n**Analyzing Queue Retry Timeout Report**\n\nInitial review focuses on /workspace/product/brief.md and /workspace/product/current.md to understand the context of the queue retry and reported timeout issue. Further investigation of the source archive is needed to correlate logs, monitor configurations and relevant code changes with timeout reports to determine if the reported issue is resolved. The current snapshot requires a detailed review of all associated records to establish a timeline and pinpoint the root cause of the timeout issues.\n\n\n**Correlating Timeouts With Prior Action**\n\nThe current timeout report necessitates correlating it with PR 781 and its subsequent rollback on July 27 to determine any connection. `/workspace/product/history/retired/queue-sentinel/actions/record-f09cf4270b.md` shows the original change, and `/workspace/product/history/evidence/record-1555a62ab3.md` captures initial observations. The rollback details are in `/workspace/product/history/retired/queue-sentinel/actions/record-c04c640916.md`. Further examination is needed to confirm if the current timeout symptoms are similar to those prior to the rollback.\n\nThe next action involves reviewing the current timeout report to ascertain if the issues are related to the tenant-aware deduplication. The uncertainty lies in establishing a direct causal link between PR 781 and the current report. Recommendation to `/workspace/work/decision.md` to begin review.\n\n\n**Assessing PR 842 Deployment Status**\n\nThe critical piece is confirming if PR 842, the queue re